— Buildings can be moved to different spots (for Luck Coins);
— A new unit — motorcyclist (in the simulator yet only);
— A new Wonder of the World "Freight airport";
Allows you to trade by air (with increased speed) with other cities that have the same Wonder of the World.
— You can set the level of the treasury balance, protected from withdrawals;
— Country head elections. Players who are absent from the game for a long period, are not counted as electors;
— Financial graph of spendings for troops trainings is implemented;
Informatorium reports can be made every 10 hours (20 hours before).

Approximate release date — October, 10th.

— Tonnels can now be built through mountains. Tonnels increase movement speed (we can't yet say for how much);
— Barter does not disappear any more. You can now switch it back on at any time;
— Water paths are 2 times shorter than land ones, river paths are 3 times shorter;
— Campus effectivity is changed: 1%/2%/3% now (2%/4%/7% before);
— Campuses additionally increase the number of work places in all scientific buildings by 2% / 4% / 6%;
— The pledge in the streams is reduced to 3 hours (5 hours before);
— Highway cost has changed: 50 population (100 before), 700 granite (500 before).

Approximate launch time — mid August.

5th world — June, 18th;
6th and 7th worlds — June, 20th.

Changes:

— Country dotations for resources production are implemented;
— Tactics conditions can now include number of troops from each side;
— Morgenstern and Robodog are available to be trained in cities;
— Amount of required MCC (Mission Control Centers) is reduced to 4 (5 before);
— Ski resort is improved (details will be announced later);

Release date is yet unknowm. But it happens not earlier then mid-june.
Changing the amount of required MCCs can not be implemented in any existing world by the request of any large country in it.

